# Expert workflow

## Parse the user prompt

Expect: **which landing** + **where** (section/file) + **what** + **how** + optional **screenshot/Figma**.
UI can differ per landing. Never force Home layout onto another route.
Rewrite vague asks into concrete tasks before coding.
Confirm assets from `brand.ts` / `site.ts`, not hardcoded paths.
Before coding a section: skim `landing-known-issues.mdc` + `assets-workflow.mdc` so prior FORJD rework bugs are not repeated.
Lock columns/gaps first (`section-build-gate.mdc`); polish second.

## Deliver

0. **Branch (must):** stay on `dev`. Before any main push: `npm run build` green → merge `dev` into `main` → `git push origin main` → sync `dev` (`git-branch-workflow.mdc` + `AGENTS.md`)
1. Components in `src/components/*`; copy in `src/data/`; keep `page.tsx` thin
2. Mobile-first; Motion stagger subtle; reuse primitives
3. SEO in `@/lib/seo` when positioning/copy changes
4. Fix visual bugs in the same pass (seams, overflow, wrong layer)

## Verify (definition of done)

- [ ] Correct folder structure (thin page, section components)
- [ ] Component-based (no markup dump in `page.tsx`)
- [ ] Matches screenshot/Figma section intent
- [ ] Mobile-first; 320 → 1280+ no horizontal scroll
- [ ] Local media / brand paths valid
- [ ] Icons + hover + badges + `cursor-pointer`; Motion used appropriately
- [ ] No new unapproved packages
- [ ] Themed **404** when shipping a full landing (`not-found.tsx` + `error.ts`)
- [ ] Scroll chrome when shipping a full landing (scrollbar + `ScrollToTop` + sticky nav)
- [ ] Brand favicon + SEO (metadata/JSON-LD/robots/sitemap) + fast-loading patterns
- [ ] `npm run build` green when claiming done

## Report

Short: what changed, files touched, pass/fail. Ask only if blocked (missing asset, conflicting designs).
